	(text "INPUTS  (4 mm banana sockets)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "08a9a9a7-d5de-49ea-ad35-24f06d55323e")
	)
	(text "HOW IT WORKS\nK1+K2 (4 poles) connect +15, -15 and GND to J14-J21. Relays off = outputs fully disconnected, all three lines.\nThe two coils in series (720 ohm) sit across +15V_IN to -15V_IN through D1 and R1 and are switched by Q1. Q1's gate is charged\nfrom GND_IN, so the relays can only close when all three leads are present, +15 is ~30 V above -15 and GND sits between them.\nEvery wrong way to plug in the three leads gives reverse voltage on the coils (blocked by D1), 15 V or less on the coils\n(below the 8.4 V must-operate per coil) or a negative gate: the relays cannot close and nothing reaches J14-J21.\nOnly one rail present (the other unplugged or switched off): no coil current, outputs stay disconnected.\nDELAY: C1 charges through R2 toward ~4.7 V on Q1's gate: the relays close about 1 s after the last rail comes up\n(0.3-1.5 s over the 2N7000 threshold spread). If -15 or GND goes away while running, C1 drains and the relays drop in ~1-2 s.\nRECOVERY: power off, fix the leads, power on. Nothing to replace.\nTH1/TH2 limit the inrush into the downstream capacitors when the contacts close, which protects the relay contacts\n(2 ohm cold, 0.1-0.3 ohm hot: ~0.3-0.6 V drop per rail at 1.5-2.5 A). Give them about a minute to cool after a quick off/on.\nSwitch the supply off before moving leads: the check happens at turn-on.\nOUTPUT CONNECTORS: Samtec HPM-03-05-T-S, pin 1 +15 V, 2 GND, 3 -15 V, same as the routing boards' P1. They are unshrouded:\na cable housing flipped end-for-end swaps +15 and -15 at that board, so key or mark the housings.\nGND_OUT is kept separate from the jacks' GND on this board: they meet at the master through its power cable and the IDC ribbons.\nRATINGS: contacts 8 A, NTC 5 A max -> about 4 A per rail in total. Coils 34 mA at +/-15 V (37 mA at +/-16.6 V), ~1 W."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 182.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0a476213-39af-4d9a-bca8-657292399a7b")
	)
	(text "POLARITY-QUALIFIED, DELAYED RELAY DRIVE"
